S1.3. Fixes a defect introduced by b60911ef and found by subagent
S2-extents while building S2; implemented by that agent, separability and
controls verified here before staging.

Separable from the extent work because neither backend needed a new
primitive: cudaSource.Barrier already emitted __syncthreads and
cudamegacpu's worker.Barrier already did the CTA wait, so the change is
one 18-line hunk in Runner.Run plus the regenerated goldens.

Control history worth keeping: the first attempt to fire the CPU gate
came back 0/20 at whole-suite granularity, and the agent reported that
rather than quoting it as a pass. It then widened to -count=200 of the
cross test alone and got a double dissociation -- barrier deleted 5/200,
8/200, 3/200; barrier present 0/600; S2 tree 0/600 and no DATA RACE.
That also retracts the earlier flake rates (3/20 at HEAD, 6/20 on the S2
tree): low-count draws of a thin Bernoulli, not a rate. Verified here:
200 draws clean on the parked barrier-only tree and on the S2 tree, and
the race that reproduced 4 of 4 runs before is gone.

The device passed 5/5 with the barrier deleted. The agent proved the
mutation was present in the artifact that passed by re-running the same
binary against the emitted-text test and failing it. Recorded as the
S0.5 blindness, not as evidence the barrier is unneeded.

Known gap, not fixed: nothing ties a committed .ptx/.sass to the .cu it
was built from. Changing a .cu and running the package still reports ok,
with every PTX assertion passing against artifacts built from the old
source.
